WEBVTT

1
00:00:32.172 --> 00:00:32.472
"Go, Whales!"

2
00:00:32.492 --> 00:00:34.333
Brooklyn Robbins cheered on her team in the Wayland Middle School gym.

3
00:00:34.353 --> 00:00:35.514
The basketball bounced from player to player.

4
00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:36.014
"Grab the ball, Dirk!

5
00:00:36.034 --> 00:00:37.015
Move!" she shouted at the team's star forward.

6
00:00:37.035 --> 00:00:38.496
Dirk raced across the court after the opposing point guard.

7
00:00:38.516 --> 00:00:40.677
Brooklyn was holding an icy water bottle.

8
00:00:41.297 --> 00:00:44.779
Just then it slipped from her hand and started rolling toward the court.

9
00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:51.243
She raced to get the bottle before it rolled under players' feet.

10
00:00:51.263 --> 00:00:54.825
"Here, Brooklyn."

11
00:00:55.365 --> 00:00:57.967
Coach Teagan grabbed the bottle and tossed it to her.

12
00:00:57.987 --> 00:01:00.168
"Thanks, Coach."

13
00:01:00.812 --> 00:01:03.313
Brooklyn fumbled the bottle, nearly dropping it.

14
00:01:04.214 --> 00:01:08.816
She'd gotten so caught up in watching the game that she'd forgotten to finish her task as the

15
00:01:08.856 --> 00:01:12.917
Whales' team manager—filling the cooler with water bottles for the players.

16
00:01:14.218 --> 00:01:16.139
Brooklyn dropped the bottle into the cooler.

17
00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:19.100
"Yikes," she thought.

18
00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:25.783
"If I can't handle water bottles, how will I ever handle coaching players in the professional leagues?"

19
00:01:26.723 --> 00:01:28.204
Brooklyn turned back to the game.

20
00:01:29.052 --> 00:01:33.975
Every Whales player was struggling to get the ball from the lead point guard on the Treton Terriers

21
00:01:34.035 --> 00:01:40.719
team. Brooklyn had silently nicknamed the guard "The Giant."

22
00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:46.722
Now The Giant was dribbling the ball as if he were the only player on the court.

23
00:01:49.624 --> 00:01:51.465
Dirk inched closer to The Giant.

24
00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:56.368
Dirk was in a perfect position for a clean shot.

25
00:01:57.036 --> 00:02:00.257
But instead of trying to steal the ball, he'd stopped moving.

26
00:02:01.537 --> 00:02:05.338
He looked stuck to the floor, holding his arms out like a scarecrow.

27
00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:07.819
"Coach, what's up with Dirk?"

28
00:02:08.219 --> 00:02:09.059
Brooklyn murmured.

29
00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.120
No answer.

30
00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.540
Coach was staring at his phone again.

31
00:02:14.201 --> 00:02:16.241
His wife was expecting triplets soon.

32
00:02:16.261 --> 00:02:18.222
"You're open, Dirk!"

33
00:02:18.602 --> 00:02:19.442
Brooklyn shouted.

34
00:02:19.462 --> 00:02:20.822
"Get the ball!"

35
00:02:20.842 --> 00:02:22.763
"Think like a Jedi!"

36
00:02:23.123 --> 00:02:24.463
Marv Lennox chimed in.

37
00:02:25.364 --> 00:02:26.664
Brooklyn grinned at Marv.

38
00:02:27.244 --> 00:02:30.426
The assistant coach scratched nervously at his gray beard.

39
00:02:30.446 --> 00:02:33.188
"Laser him!"

40
00:02:33.688 --> 00:02:35.169
cried another Whales player.

41
00:02:35.829 --> 00:02:39.091
Everyone at Wayland knew Dirk loved the Star Wars movies.

42
00:02:39.791 --> 00:02:41.352
Maybe this would get him moving.

43
00:02:42.313 --> 00:02:42.833
It didn't.

44
00:02:43.474 --> 00:02:47.496
The Giant sailed past Dirk and threw a shot from center court.

45
00:02:50.038 --> 00:02:53.159
The ball whisked through the hoop, and the crowd cheered.

46
00:02:57.144 --> 00:02:58.085
Brooklyn clapped.

47
00:02:58.105 --> 00:03:01.087
"Great three-pointer!"

48
00:03:01.107 --> 00:03:04.649
"Brooklyn, don't cheer for the enemy."

49
00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:10.854
Jacey had been sitting slumped on the sidelines after missing a free throw during the game's first quarter.

50
00:03:11.594 --> 00:03:13.235
She pulled her ponytail tighter.

51
00:03:13.255 --> 00:03:15.617
"This is a game, Jacey.

52
00:03:15.657 --> 00:03:18.079
There are no enemies," Brooklyn said.

53
00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.721
Brooklyn had known Jacey since preschool.

54
00:03:22.281 --> 00:03:25.664
But Jacey seemed different now that the girls were in middle school.

55
00:03:26.856 --> 00:03:30.898
She didn't text Brooklyn very often anymore or invite her to do things.

56
00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:34.919
The girls were still friends, just not close friends.

57
00:03:37.721 --> 00:03:41.622
The Whales were ten points behind when the halftime buzzer blared.

58
00:03:42.402 --> 00:03:47.525
Coach Teagan should've been rousing the tired players, but he had gone off to phone his wife.

59
00:03:50.866 --> 00:03:53.467
Marv took over trying to boost the team's morale.

60
00:03:53.487 --> 00:03:55.688
"You guys have to focus out there."

61
00:03:56.384 --> 00:03:58.084
He pointed at Stuart and Jacey.

62
00:03:58.105 --> 00:04:01.845
"The offense must push the other team's dribblers back.

63
00:04:02.346 --> 00:04:05.646
Dirk, use your height to jump and block whenever you can.

64
00:04:06.447 --> 00:04:09.968
Remember—this is our last regular game before play-offs start.

65
00:04:10.508 --> 00:04:11.908
We could use a win today."

66
00:04:12.848 --> 00:04:15.309
Brooklyn had been scooping up loose basketballs.

67
00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:23.251
When she saw the Whales' players sitting with their heads down, she jumped into the circle next to

68
00:04:23.291 --> 00:04:26.172
Marv—and accidentally stomped on his foot.

69
00:04:27.148 --> 00:04:29.129
"Oof!" He stumbled backward.

70
00:04:29.149 --> 00:04:30.490
"Sorry, Marv!"

71
00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:31.471
Brooklyn said.

72
00:04:31.491 --> 00:04:33.031
"I've got an idea."

73
00:04:34.032 --> 00:04:35.072
Marv rubbed his foot.

74
00:04:35.093 --> 00:04:37.914
"Let's hear it, Brooklyn."

75
00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:41.316
"Don't let that tall guard near the ball.

76
00:04:42.016 --> 00:04:44.017
He's moving better than everyone today.

77
00:04:44.598 --> 00:04:52.642
He dribbles She started to gesture with her arms, dropping all the balls she was holding.

78
00:04:53.582 --> 00:04:54.863
Dirk burst out laughing.

79
00:04:56.912 --> 00:05:00.314
"Everyone moves better than you, klutz!"

80
00:05:01.235 --> 00:05:03.577
Jacey and a few other players laughed too.

81
00:05:03.597 --> 00:05:06.238
"I'm graceful inside!"

82
00:05:06.719 --> 00:05:09.080
Brooklyn said quickly, forcing a smile.

83
00:05:10.201 --> 00:05:11.222
Marv was frowning.

84
00:05:11.242 --> 00:05:13.884
"Dirk, apologize to Brooklyn."

85
00:05:14.524 --> 00:05:16.025
There was a long silence.

86
00:05:18.347 --> 00:05:20.748
"Now!" the assistant coach said.

87
00:05:20.768 --> 00:05:23.450
"Sorry," Dirk mumbled.

88
00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:25.952
"Thank you," Marv said.

89
00:05:26.484 --> 00:05:28.725
"And thanks for the tip on that guard, Brooklyn."

90
00:05:30.006 --> 00:05:30.906
Brooklyn nodded.

91
00:05:30.926 --> 00:05:35.028
"Don't let Dirk's insult get to you," she told herself.

92
00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:42.812
At basketball camp last year, her counselor had said, "Some players are big, some small, some fast, some

93
00:05:42.892 --> 00:05:47.554
slow. But if you play smart, you can score hoops against anyone."

94
00:05:48.334 --> 00:05:54.721
It had taken time for Brooklyn to understand what her counselor meant, especially with bullies calling her "clumsy

95
00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:57.381
oaf" or "klutz" throughout elementary school.

96
00:05:58.302 --> 00:06:03.163
Since arriving at Wayland Middle School for sixth grade, Brooklyn had lived for basketball.

97
00:06:04.203 --> 00:06:09.485
Making the Whales team was nearly impossible, with the way she moved and her small size.

98
00:06:10.445 --> 00:06:15.907
But working as the Whales' team manager was her first step to achieving her dream of becoming a

99
00:06:15.967 --> 00:06:16.787
coach one day.

100
00:06:19.748 --> 00:06:23.214
After halftime the Terriers quickly scored another three-pointer.

101
00:06:25.616 --> 00:06:28.779
Marv and Coach Teagan called the Whales in for a time-out.

102
00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:31.481
Brooklyn tugged on Marv's sleeve.

103
00:06:31.501 --> 00:06:35.925
"What about that special play I showed everyone in practice last week?

104
00:06:36.425 --> 00:06:37.166
The loop play?"

105
00:06:38.107 --> 00:06:38.907
Dirk scowled.

106
00:06:38.927 --> 00:06:40.309
"Dumb play."

107
00:06:40.329 --> 00:06:43.992
"Dirk!" Coach Teagan looked up from texting.

108
00:06:44.012 --> 00:06:47.234
"This is your last warning to be respectful."

109
00:06:47.755 --> 00:06:48.716
He turned to the team.

110
00:06:49.292 --> 00:06:50.753
"Brooklyn's idea is good.

111
00:06:50.893 --> 00:06:51.994
We've got to mix it up."

112
00:06:52.795 --> 00:06:57.058
Dirk nodded and mumbled another apology, but he was still scowling.

113
00:06:57.998 --> 00:07:03.502
Coach Teagan put one hand out and each player layered a hand on top for the team cheer.

114
00:07:03.522 --> 00:07:06.824
"Whales Whoosh!"

115
00:07:07.305 --> 00:07:08.005
they shouted.

116
00:07:09.466 --> 00:07:12.689
The Whales' first try with the loop play failed.

117
00:07:12.709 --> 00:07:17.252
"Foul!" The official pointed at Dirk.

118
00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:19.901
He'd slammed into his giant opponent.

119
00:07:19.921 --> 00:07:22.422
"Play smart, Dirk!"

120
00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:23.843
Brooklyn shouted.

121
00:07:25.083 --> 00:07:27.744
A Whales player dribbled and passed the ball to Dirk.

122
00:07:30.185 --> 00:07:32.206
The team was trying the loop play again.

123
00:07:32.906 --> 00:07:34.767
Brooklyn ran down the sidelines.

124
00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:37.508
"Go, Dirk!"

125
00:07:38.248 --> 00:07:40.309
She bumped into someone near the team bench.

126
00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:43.110
It was Jacey.

127
00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:45.711
"Sorry," Brooklyn said.

128
00:07:45.731 --> 00:07:47.668
"It's okay."

129
00:07:47.688 --> 00:07:49.169
Jacey moved in front of Brooklyn.

130
00:07:49.189 --> 00:07:52.370
"Yeah, Dirk!"

131
00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:57.212
Brooklyn saw Dirk was now midcourt, with a clear shot to the basket.

132
00:07:57.232 --> 00:07:58.613
"Shoot it!

133
00:07:58.633 --> 00:07:59.413
You've got this!"

134
00:07:59.873 --> 00:08:00.594
Marv yelled.

135
00:08:01.494 --> 00:08:03.595
Dirk raced across the court, dribbling.

136
00:08:06.556 --> 00:08:09.037
Suddenly The Giant lunged for the ball.

137
00:08:13.019 --> 00:08:14.479
it!" Brooklyn called.

138
00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:15.900
Dirk looked up.

139
00:08:16.576 --> 00:08:21.137
Brooklyn hoped he'd heard her, but the crowd was loud—really loud.

140
00:08:21.157 --> 00:08:25.238
"Loop! Loop!"

141
00:08:25.698 --> 00:08:27.079
Marv and Coach shouted.

142
00:08:27.719 --> 00:08:32.660
Dirk turned, but he went the wrong direction, toward the other team's basket.

143
00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:37.002
"Go left, Dirk!"

144
00:08:37.542 --> 00:08:41.343
Brooklyn flung out her arms, accidentally whacking Jacey.

145
00:08:41.363 --> 00:08:44.183
"Ow!" Jacey cried.

146
00:08:44.203 --> 00:08:46.800
"Sorry, Jacey!

147
00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:49.761
I—" Just then Dirk swiveled sideways with the basketball.

148
00:08:52.202 --> 00:08:56.963
Unable to weave through the players blocking center court, he bolted down the sideline.

149
00:08:59.604 --> 00:09:03.205
The Giant lunged for the ball again, slamming into Dirk.

150
00:09:05.445 --> 00:09:06.406
The buzzer blared.

151
00:09:09.126 --> 00:09:14.028
The game was over, but Dirk was still moving, and moving too fast to stop.

152
00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:19.766
He stumbled off the court—and crashed straight into Brooklyn.
